# DO NOT DELETE THIS FILE. It looks unreferenced. It is not.
#
# Nothing in this repository names it, because its only consumer is the
# OPENVPN_CONFIG *secret*, which holds this file's path and is passed to
# `config_file:` on kota65535/github-openvpn-connect-action in build-deploy.yml.
# A repo-wide grep therefore finds no references at all.
#
# Commit 09a61db deleted it on exactly that reasoning, and every deploy since
# has failed at "Connect to VPN" with `config file '***' not found` -- masked,
# so the error does not even name the missing path. Restored here from
# trencho/air-quality-rest-api, which uses the identical wiring and works.
#
# Before deleting anything that appears unused in this repo, check the secrets,
# the workflows and the deploy host, not just the working tree.
#
# There is NO key material below, which is what makes it safe to commit to a
# public repo: `ca`, `cert` and `tls-crypt` are paths to files build-deploy.yml
# writes at runtime from the CA_CERT, CLIENT_CERT and TLS_CRYPT_KEY secrets, and
# the client private key is supplied separately through the action's
# `client_key:` input from USER_KEY. Keep it that way -- never inline a <key>
# block here.
client
dev tun
proto udp
remote 194.149.144.244 11194
resolv-retry infinite
nobind
persist-key
persist-tun
remote-cert-tls server
auth SHA512
cipher AES-256-GCM
ignore-unknown-option block-outside-dns
block-outside-dns
verb 3
ca /etc/openvpn/ca.crt
cert /etc/openvpn/client.crt
tls-crypt /etc/openvpn/tls-crypt.key
